   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gates_to_Purgatory",
   "resumo_en": "Gates to Purgatory is the debut studio album by German heavy metal band Running Wild, released in 1984. Predating their pirate themes, the album features mostly satanically-influenced lyrics, alongside songs with anarchic and libertarian (in the sense of European libertarianism) themes. The lyrical content was partly influenced by Gerald \"Preacher\" Warnecke's studies in theology. He left the band shortly after the album's release to become a vicar.\nDespite not being actively promoted, the album sold over 20,000 copies within the first three months, and influenced several other bands worldwide.\nIt was reissued in 2012 by Lemon Records and in 2017 by Noise Records.",
